{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:cf787332cff18848b9304205444f382bd150bf0e9a9f2e7e8bda45689c4acb57","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026#cor:separable-products","title":"Separable products and simultaneous values"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/4ea9037187ece0a2e6540abc.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Corollary","generation_id":"sha256:eb85d3603ec7254e8723f8292d2014fbb295087c537d4a9a7c22689061a82822","id":"r:Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026:cor:separable-products","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026","name":"Separable products and simultaneous values","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"1.3","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/sections/01-introduction.tex","label":"cor:separable-products","line":136,"manuscript":"Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026","statement_sha256":"f9fa373e0a933e36b6a0d928797a8e3fe5c8d6a71397c72e546b7fbe3a8779e6"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026.html#cor:separable-products","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:8baa9ae26dbc52c65a40a3268770624b6398bb16806f0cee743b9de348f90526","file":"preprints/Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":136,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"f9fa373e0a933e36b6a0d928797a8e3fe5c8d6a71397c72e546b7fbe3a8779e6","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:8baa9ae26dbc52c65a40a3268770624b6398bb16806f0cee743b9de348f90526","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L136"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:separable-products}\nFix an integer $k\\ge2$. Let $F\\in\\Z[x]\\setminus\\{0\\}$ be separable over\n$\\Q$, with every nonconstant irreducible factor of degree at most $k+2$.\nIf $\\rho_F(p^k)<p^k$ for every prime $p$, then\n\\[\n S_{F,k}(N)=c_{F,k}N+o_{F,k}(N),\\qquad\n c_{F,k}=\\prod_p\\left(1-\\frac{\\rho_F(p^k)}{p^k}\\right)>0.\n\\]\nMore generally, let $\\mathbf F=(F_1,\\ldots,F_r)$, with $r\\ge1$, be a fixed\nfamily of nonzero integer polynomials, each separable over $\\Q$ with all\nnonconstant irreducible factors of degree at most $k+2$. Factors may be\nshared by different $F_i$. Put\n\\[\n \\Omega_p=\\{a\\in\\Z/p^k\\Z:p^k\\mid F_i(a)\\text{ for at least one }i\\}.\n\\]\nLet $S_{\\mathbf F,k}(N)$ count the integers $1\\le n\\le N$ for which every\n$F_i(n)$ is $k$-power-free. If $\\#\\Omega_p<p^k$ for every prime $p$, then\n\\[\n S_{\\mathbf F,k}(N)=c_{\\mathbf F,k}N+o_{\\mathbf F,k}(N),\\qquad\n c_{\\mathbf F,k}=\\prod_p\\left(1-\\frac{\\#\\Omega_p}{p^k}\\right)>0.\n\\]"}
